laytime_at_review": 410, "last_played": 1727317523, "avatar": "933860e5e7817b0fcb301f52c49fe266328fec3d"}, "language": "english", "review": "When Space Marine first came out, I didn’t give it the credit it deserved. I didn’t know much about Warhammer 40k, so I just wrote it off as another Gears of War-style shooter. Yeah… heresy, I know.\n\nBut after getting into the Warhammer universe over the years, coming back to this game just hits different. Playing as an Adeptus Astartes isn’t just fun anymore, it feels like stepping into something legendary. The weight of the armor, the chainsword, the righteous fury… it all clicks when you know what it means to be a Space Marine.\n\nThe story’s not groundbreaking on its own, but once you’re invested in the lore, it’s awesome getting to purge a planet of Orks and Chaos. The power fantasy works, and the game gives you just enough tools to feel like an unstoppable force while still keeping the combat engaging.\n\nIt’s not perfect, and yeah, it shows its age in places, but I had a blast revisiting it. For fans of 40k, or folks finally learning to appreciate it like I did, this one’s worth your time.\n\nFOR THE EMPEROR!\n\nEnjoyed this? Follow for more dad-approved recs! Light in the Lobby: https://store.steampowered.com/curator/45756112-Light-in-the-Lobby/", "timestamp_created": 1727727886, "timestamp_updated": 1760721981, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": true, "app_release_date": "1315281600", "reactions": []}]}